 36S 3c  MeV {+37}Cl beams produced from the Argonne Tandem Linac Accelerator   
 36S 4c  System (ATLAS). Targets were 1 mg/cm{+2} 98.1% enriched {+160}Gd backed
 36S 5c  by 15 mg/cm{+2} gold. |g rays were detected using the Argonne-Notre    
 36S 6c  Dame BGO |g-ray facility consisting of 12 Compton-suppressed Ge        
 36S 7c  detectors and a 50-element bismuth germanate (BGO) array. Measured E|g,
 36S 8c  I|g, and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels. |g|g-coin gates were placed on     
 36S 9c  known |g rays in specific A|?160 products to select individual reaction
 36S Ac  channels and identify coincident |g rays in light product partners.    
 36S Bc  |g|g-correlation matrices produced with the fold condition 4 |< k |< 9 
 36S Cc  were found to include most of the events associated with deep-inelastic
 36S Dc  processes.                                                             
