 36S  c  2022Gr07: A 215-MeV {+36}S beam was produced from the XTU-Tandem       
 36S 2c  ALPI-superconducting linear accelerator complex at the INFN Legnaro    
 36S 3c  National Laboratory, Italy. The target was 1-mg/cm{+2} 99.7% enriched  
 36S 4c  {+208}Pb with 1 mg/cm{+2} Nb backing and mounted onto the Cologne      
 36S 5c  differential plunger. Projectile-like fragments produced in binary     
 36S 6c  grazing reactions were separated and identified by the PRISMA          
 36S 7c  spectrometer. |g rays were detected using the AGATA demonstrator array 
 36S 8c  of five triple cluster modules of 36-fold segmented Ge crystals        
 36S 9c  covering backward angles from 135|' to 175|'. Measured E|g with Doppler
 36S Ac  corrections, ({+36}S)|g-coin, and level lifetimes using the            
 36S Bc  differential recoil-distance method (DRDM). Compared with shell-model  
 36S Cc  calculations. Measured E|g, I|g, fragment-|g-coin, recoil distance.    
 36S Dc  Deduced levels, lifetimes. Compared with shell-model calculations with 
 36S Ec  PSDPF, SDPF-U, and FSU effective interactions. Preliminary results are 
 36S Fc  given in 2005Ol04.                                                     
 36S  c  2010WaZT: A 215-MeV {+36}S{+9} beam was produced from the XTU-Tandem   
 36S 2c  ALPI-superconducting linear accelerator complex at the INFN Legnaro    
 36S 3c  National Laboratory, Italy. The target was 300-|mg/cm{+2}, 99.7%       
 36S 4c  enriched {+208}Pb with 20-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Projectile-like   
 36S 5c  fragments produced in binary grazing reactions were separated and      
 36S 6c  identified by the PRISMA spectrometer. |g rays were detected using the 
 36S 7c  CLARA array of 22 escape-suppressed Ge clover detectors covering the   
 36S 8c  azimuthal angles from 98|' to 180|'. Measured E|g with Doppler         
 36S 9c  corrections, I|g, and ({+36}S)|g-coin. Deduced levels. Compared with   
 36S Ac  shell-model calculations. Also see 2010Wa12 paper, partial results of  
 36S Bc  2010WaZT Thesis.                                                       
