 36S  c  2008Sp01: {+12}C({+36}S,{+36}S'|g) with E=70 MeV {+36}S beam provided  
 36S 2c  from the Cologne accelerator facility on a multi-layer target of 0.19  
 36S 3c  mg/cm{+2} natural C, 3.03 mg/cm{+2} Gd, 1.0 mg/cm{+2} Ta, and 2.0      
 36S 4c  mg/cm{+2} Cu. The Gd layer was cooled to liquid-nitrogen temperature   
 36S 5c  and magnetized to saturation by a 0.06-T external field.               
 36S 6c  Forward-scattered {+12}C ions from Coulomb excitation and |a particles 
 36S 7c  from {+8}Be via |a-transfer reaction {+12}C({+36}S,{+8}Be){+40}Ar were 
 36S 8c  detected by a 300-mm{+2} Si counter at 0|'. |g rays were measured by   
 36S 9c  four 12.7|*12.7-cm NaI(Tl) scintillators at 65|' and 115|' and by a 40%
 36S Ac  Ge detector at 0|'. Measured E|g, I|g, particle-|g coin, counting-rate 
 36S Bc  double ratio, and particle-|g angular-correlation slope. Deduced       
 36S Cc  precession angles, g factors using the transient field technique, and  
 36S Dc  lifetimes from DSAM lineshape analysis. Calculated B(E2)|^ from their  
 36S Ec  measured lifetimes. Compared with OXBASH shell-model calculations using
 36S Fc  the WBT interaction in the sdfp space.                                 
